{"skill":{"slug":"node-connect","displayName":"node-connect"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1774453555202,"changelog":"Initial registration","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4649,"sha256":"3b89d261b5737609df82ee7ad41e8464065a334f17d803b420507c092ed0f321","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1988,"sha256":"d9ec2de2a44ecd91f9e325fb25fcfe48ceed758cc1846231b89ef94f263b2347","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789435923627,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"f3b77824fc1c0735d80497c0c147ecd0603fad83a3b4a5e350d25abf86126d75","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/f3b77824fc1c0735d80497c0c147ecd0603fad83a3b4a5e350d25abf86126d75","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780086581641},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789435923627},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is mostly coherent troubleshooting guidance, but it recommends approving the latest pending device pairing without verifying the device identity.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Read-only diagnostic commands and route checks are proportionate, but the device approval command mutates authorization state and may grant access to a paired companion device.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact is a single Markdown skill file with no executable scripts, bundled dependencies, install hooks, or remote payload retrieval.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"For a 'pairing required' state, the skill instructs running `openclaw devices approve --latest` after listing devices, and later says pending requests should be approved first, without requiring the user to verify the intended device, request ID, fingerprint, or pairing code.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Approving a device can create persistent trusted access for that device; the guidance does not scope approval to a verified request or describe rejecting ambiguous or unknown pending requests.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The capability fits the stated purpose of diagnosing OpenClaw node connection and pairing failures, including checking QR route configuration, gateway settings, Tailscale status, device lists, and node status.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this skill before installing. Its diagnostics are ordinary for OpenClaw connection troubleshooting, but do not approve a device solely because it is the latest pending request. Compare the pending request with the intended device using a stable request ID, displayed code, fingerprint, or other identifier, and reject unknown or ambiguous requests before approving anything.","findings":"[T05] expected: Device approval is relevant to OpenClaw pairing troubleshooting, but the artifact-backed concern is valid because selecting `--latest` can approve the wrong pending request and the instructions omit identity verification before authorization.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789435923627}}}}}